WEBVTT

00:00:06.800 --> 00:00:08.880
Oh no! Oh no!

00:00:09.170 --> 00:00:10.880
Oh my gosh!

00:00:11.840 --> 00:00:12.930
What's going on?

00:00:12.930 --> 00:00:14.640
Is something broken
in the engine department?

00:00:14.930 --> 00:00:15.890
No!

00:00:16.220 --> 00:00:18.010
Is one of the engineers sick?

00:00:18.010 --> 00:00:19.470
Everyone's fine!

00:00:19.600 --> 00:00:20.640
Then what is it?

00:00:21.060 --> 00:00:23.520
The Harekaze has crossed the equator!

00:00:24.770 --> 00:00:25.770
The equator?

00:00:27.570 --> 00:00:28.530
As a matter of fact,

00:00:28.730 --> 00:00:29.730
we have.

00:00:30.110 --> 00:00:32.150
Equator Festival!

00:00:32.740 --> 00:00:34.530
Equator Festival?

00:00:34.860 --> 00:00:37.120
Festival! Festival!

00:02:11.000 --> 00:02:13.880
Since the ship is undergoing repairs anyway,

00:02:13.880 --> 00:02:16.260
I'd like to have an Equator Festival!

00:02:16.550 --> 00:02:18.090
Equator Festival?

00:02:18.090 --> 00:02:20.510
Another randomly named event.

00:02:20.800 --> 00:02:24.720
What are you talking about? Equator Festivals
have an ancient and honorable origin!

00:02:24.970 --> 00:02:27.310
What is their ancient and honorable origin?

00:02:27.730 --> 00:02:30.770
For that, Kuro, you can explain!

00:02:31.020 --> 00:02:34.860
It began in the great sailing era, when a ship
couldn't move if the wind wasn't blowing.

00:02:35.780 --> 00:02:39.780
When a ship was in
an area of calm near the equator,

00:02:39.780 --> 00:02:43.030
the crew would pray
to the god of the sea for safe passage.

00:02:44.330 --> 00:02:49.210
There are historical records of crew members
having masquerades and performing in skits,

00:02:49.210 --> 00:02:52.250
in a festival-like atmosphere
when their ship crossed the equator.

00:02:54.050 --> 00:02:54.800
Huh...

00:02:54.800 --> 00:02:56.090
Really.

00:02:56.420 --> 00:03:00.300
Chief Engineer Yanagiwara
has volunteered to be in charge.

00:03:00.720 --> 00:03:02.800
- I'm not surprised.
- Seriously?

00:03:03.260 --> 00:03:06.140
Everyone! Let's get charged up for this!

00:03:06.140 --> 00:03:08.690
Think up some kind of performance you can do!

00:03:08.810 --> 00:03:11.190
The festival is the day after tomorrow!

00:03:12.270 --> 00:03:13.820
How bothersome.

00:03:14.900 --> 00:03:15.900
Are you okay?

00:03:16.190 --> 00:03:16.900
Fine here.

00:03:17.030 --> 00:03:19.070
We replenished everything you needed.

00:03:19.400 --> 00:03:23.030
It'll take a couple more days
to switch out the main battery, though.

00:03:23.030 --> 00:03:25.950
Thank you. I troubled you again, huh?

00:03:26.160 --> 00:03:30.370
Not at all. We heard all about
the Harekaze's exploits.

00:03:30.830 --> 00:03:35.460
You ran the Hiei aground, and were
successful boarding the Spee.

00:03:35.460 --> 00:03:40.220
I had the impression your crew was a collection
of oddballs, but you guys are amazing.

00:03:42.050 --> 00:03:43.220
Thank you.

00:03:43.390 --> 00:03:44.970
What performance should we do?

00:03:46.430 --> 00:03:48.560
We have to do something?

00:03:49.520 --> 00:03:51.270
Can I think of something for us?

00:03:51.270 --> 00:03:52.150
No.

00:03:52.980 --> 00:03:57.610
I have a feeling we wouldn't be able
to carry out whatever Coco had in mind.

00:03:57.820 --> 00:04:00.490
Then think of something with me, Shiro!

00:04:00.490 --> 00:04:01.610
Let go!

00:04:01.360 --> 00:04:04.030
Somewhere along the line,
she's become attached.

00:04:01.910 --> 00:04:03.870
Sorry, you're stuck with me!

00:04:04.030 --> 00:04:06.200
What's with this annoying distance?

00:04:04.030 --> 00:04:06.200
- Won't you let go?
- I won't, see!

00:04:06.200 --> 00:04:07.160
Aye...

00:04:06.200 --> 00:04:08.790
- I'm tellin' ya!
- I ain't!

00:04:07.540 --> 00:04:09.370
Huh? Are they in perfect harmony?

00:04:09.370 --> 00:04:10.370
Com'on now!

00:04:09.540 --> 00:04:10.370
Yeah.

00:04:13.420 --> 00:04:18.130
The inspection results show the students who
were infected by the virus are back to normal.

00:04:18.130 --> 00:04:20.880
The Harekaze's mission
regarding the Spee was a success.

00:04:21.220 --> 00:04:22.630
That's incredible.

00:04:22.840 --> 00:04:23.890
They deserve a commendation.

00:04:24.300 --> 00:04:26.930
We mustn't be outdone by students.

00:04:27.180 --> 00:04:30.390
We're going to carry out Operation: Perseus.

00:04:30.730 --> 00:04:34.150
Right now, production of
the antibody is speedily underway.

00:04:34.270 --> 00:04:37.110
As soon as it's done, we're all going into action.

00:04:37.770 --> 00:04:42.240
The Choukai, the Maya and the Isuzu have
already been taken over by Mafuyu's squad.

00:04:42.650 --> 00:04:48.120
That leaves the Suzukaze, the Amatsukaze,
the Isokaze, the Tokitsukaze,

00:04:48.120 --> 00:04:50.450
and then, the Musashi.

00:04:52.210 --> 00:04:55.710
According to Mafuyu's squad,
the Musashi's last-known location

00:04:55.710 --> 00:04:58.920
was south of Ulithi on a westerly course.

00:04:58.920 --> 00:05:01.920
We believe it's heading for the Philippines.

00:05:01.920 --> 00:05:04.760
Y118_ MUSASHI

00:05:02.420 --> 00:05:04.760
However, its current position is unknown.

00:05:06.930 --> 00:05:11.390
The Blue Mermaids are leading
an operation to intercept it,

00:05:11.390 --> 00:05:15.100
but we've received a request asking
for cooperation from the student ships, too.

00:05:15.650 --> 00:05:18.900
I don't want to put a burden on the students...

00:05:18.900 --> 00:05:22.150
but we have to prevent the spread
of infection at all costs.

00:05:22.440 --> 00:05:23.450
The state of the ships?

00:05:24.320 --> 00:05:29.990
The Kazahaya, the Akikaze, the Hamakaze, and
the Maikaze have all returned to the school.

00:05:30.580 --> 00:05:35.540
The Nagara, the Urakaze, the Hagikaze, and
the Tanikaze are still doing reconnaissance.

00:05:35.790 --> 00:05:39.960
And the Mamiya and Akashi
are currently repairing the Harekaze.

00:05:40.670 --> 00:05:42.920
How are the Harekaze students doing?

00:05:43.470 --> 00:05:47.840
Their captain has sent us a report saying
they're preparing for an Equator Festival.

00:05:50.720 --> 00:05:54.350
Let them know that once repairs are done,
they will be cooperating with the mission.

00:05:54.350 --> 00:05:55.350
Yes, ma'am.

00:05:55.350 --> 00:05:57.020
TWO DAYS LATER

00:06:04.780 --> 00:06:06.070
Boom! Boom!

00:06:08.070 --> 00:06:08.990
That's freezing!

00:06:13.830 --> 00:06:15.710
This week's fortune...

00:06:15.870 --> 00:06:17.920
Scorpio is in tenth place?

00:06:18.040 --> 00:06:19.920
Taurus is 11th.

00:06:19.920 --> 00:06:21.960
At least it's not last place.

00:06:22.340 --> 00:06:24.260
You three help, too!

00:06:24.260 --> 00:06:27.050
It's too hot, so I don't want to move!

00:06:31.260 --> 00:06:33.600
This is a tall order.

00:06:34.100 --> 00:06:36.480
We've got to have food carts!

00:06:36.640 --> 00:06:38.900
Like with yakisoba and takoyaki?

00:06:38.900 --> 00:06:42.480
The old standards are fine,
but I want something with 'suka flavor!

00:06:43.020 --> 00:06:43.940
Suka?

00:06:43.940 --> 00:06:45.990
I think she's referring to "Yokosuka."

00:06:45.990 --> 00:06:48.490
Got it. We'll put our heads together.

00:06:48.820 --> 00:06:52.490
Hey, does Budgeting have any
wooden boxes that is no longer needed?

00:06:52.490 --> 00:06:53.490
We do.

00:06:54.120 --> 00:06:55.790
Are they for a performance?

00:06:55.790 --> 00:06:59.620
Nope. There's something
I want to make as a personal project.

00:07:00.540 --> 00:07:02.290
A "personal project" ?

00:07:02.290 --> 00:07:04.000
That's. A. Secret.

00:07:06.510 --> 00:07:08.010
Why? Why?!

00:07:08.260 --> 00:07:10.680
I don't like secrets!

00:07:10.260 --> 00:07:12.010
Maybe a little more to the right?

00:07:12.140 --> 00:07:13.140
There you go!

00:07:14.100 --> 00:07:15.020
Go for it!

00:07:15.350 --> 00:07:16.980
What are you doing?

00:07:16.980 --> 00:07:18.180
Watermelon splitting!

00:07:18.180 --> 00:07:21.270
Ms. Marikouji is great at this.
She never misses!

00:07:21.600 --> 00:07:23.480
What about the Equator Festival?

00:07:23.480 --> 00:07:25.820
Have you decided what kind
of performance you're going to do?

00:07:25.820 --> 00:07:27.030
Not yet.

00:07:27.030 --> 00:07:28.150
Then this is no time for—

00:07:28.150 --> 00:07:29.150
Here I go!

00:07:34.740 --> 00:07:36.120
Right down the middle!

00:07:37.250 --> 00:07:40.080
Ms. Marikouji is a master at all kinds of things!

00:07:40.670 --> 00:07:41.790
Want some, Chief Engineer?

00:07:42.080 --> 00:07:44.090
No, I don't want any of that!

00:07:45.710 --> 00:07:48.800
What are they fooling around for
when there's hardly any time to prepare—

00:07:50.930 --> 00:07:52.140
Sorry, Chief Engineer!

00:07:52.140 --> 00:07:54.930
If you have time to play,
use it to prepare for the festival!

00:07:55.760 --> 00:07:58.430
But, no one's charged up in every direction.

00:07:58.930 --> 00:08:01.730
N-No one's charged up?

00:08:01.730 --> 00:08:04.560
A water gun tournament is more fun,
don't you think?

00:08:09.860 --> 00:08:11.320
Wh-What's everyone doing?

00:08:16.490 --> 00:08:19.000
B-Break time is over!

00:08:19.750 --> 00:08:20.910
Prepare, prepare!

00:08:20.910 --> 00:08:23.880
Where am I supposed to stick this again?

00:08:23.880 --> 00:08:25.170
Festival! Festival!

00:08:25.170 --> 00:08:27.840
You don't have to fake it for my sake.

00:08:29.380 --> 00:08:31.300
I read you loud and clear.

00:08:32.180 --> 00:08:34.590
Nobody cares about the Equator Festival!

00:08:35.100 --> 00:08:40.850
Maron... Th-That's not true! We're all
looking forward to the Equator Festival!

00:08:40.850 --> 00:08:42.230
I'm totally looking forward to it!

00:08:42.230 --> 00:08:43.600
Yay! Yay!

00:08:45.020 --> 00:08:46.360
Don't force yourselves.

00:08:46.820 --> 00:08:49.400
I don't want your sympathy!

00:08:50.400 --> 00:08:51.400
Maron!

00:08:52.320 --> 00:08:55.620
Shiro, how do you think I should continue?

00:08:55.990 --> 00:08:58.160
I don't really care.

00:08:58.160 --> 00:08:59.450
You're abandoning me?

00:08:59.870 --> 00:09:02.120
Everything's as usual, huh, Coco.

00:09:02.290 --> 00:09:03.080
<i>Captain.</i>

00:09:04.000 --> 00:09:05.830
<i>You have a message from the principal.</i>

00:09:05.960 --> 00:09:07.090
Read it, Tsugu.

00:09:07.710 --> 00:09:13.170
<i>"As soon as the repairs are done, cooperate
with the Blue Mermaids on Operation: Perseus.</i>

00:09:13.170 --> 00:09:16.090
<i>Join the second rear corps." Looks like that's it.</i>

00:09:16.590 --> 00:09:17.600
Got it.

00:09:18.100 --> 00:09:21.100
They're really starting to eradicate the virus.

00:09:22.020 --> 00:09:24.640
How many other ships need to wake up?

00:09:24.640 --> 00:09:26.270
Five ships, right?

00:09:26.270 --> 00:09:30.030
They know the location of four of those ships,
but the Musashi is still missing.

00:09:36.360 --> 00:09:37.370
Captain!

00:09:37.620 --> 00:09:39.240
Kuro, what is it?

00:09:39.780 --> 00:09:41.870
Nothing. It's just, the Chief Engineer...

00:09:42.660 --> 00:09:43.870
Did something happen to Maron?

00:09:45.460 --> 00:09:46.620
She's pouting.

00:09:56.890 --> 00:09:58.510
What are you making?

00:09:58.510 --> 00:10:01.140
You'll see when I'm done!

00:10:01.970 --> 00:10:06.900
I see. So when everyone else wasn't excited
enough to her liking, she went into sulk mode.

00:10:07.230 --> 00:10:12.280
She's usually high-spirited, but once
she gets pouty, she won't budge an inch.

00:10:12.610 --> 00:10:17.030
I see. Kuro, you've been
with Maron since middle school, right?

00:10:17.360 --> 00:10:21.030
This is my fault too, for leaving
the whole festival in her hands.

00:10:21.700 --> 00:10:25.000
If she sleeps on it for a night,
she's usually in a better mood,

00:10:25.000 --> 00:10:27.420
but I don't know how to cheer her up.

00:10:27.420 --> 00:10:28.580
Listen...

00:10:29.290 --> 00:10:33.800
Maybe everyone will get fired up
with my personal project that I made.

00:10:34.340 --> 00:10:36.260
What you made, Hime?

00:10:41.510 --> 00:10:42.810
I thought I'd find you here.

00:10:43.310 --> 00:10:45.140
I'm surprised you did.

00:10:45.140 --> 00:10:49.150
Maron, whenever you sulk,
you hide out in the ship's hold.

00:10:49.150 --> 00:10:50.560
Is that right?

00:10:50.980 --> 00:10:51.980
Come with me.

00:10:52.820 --> 00:10:54.820
I've got something that will make you happy.

00:10:55.110 --> 00:10:56.190
Yakiniku?

00:10:56.190 --> 00:10:57.740
It's not food.

00:10:57.740 --> 00:10:58.910
Canned pineapple?

00:10:58.910 --> 00:11:00.740
That's food too, isn't it?

00:11:00.740 --> 00:11:01.740
Well, what is it?

00:11:01.740 --> 00:11:03.280
You'll see if you follow me.

00:11:04.830 --> 00:11:07.580
Heave-ho! Heave-ho! Heave-ho!

00:11:15.880 --> 00:11:18.090
What is this? What's going on?

00:11:18.340 --> 00:11:20.680
With more energy, Deputy-Cap!

00:11:21.800 --> 00:11:24.100
Where did you find a palanquin?

00:11:24.100 --> 00:11:25.720
I made it!

00:11:25.720 --> 00:11:28.980
So this is what your personal project was?

00:11:29.310 --> 00:11:34.610
My parents were born in Kanda, so when
I hear "festival," my blood starts racing.

00:11:34.770 --> 00:11:36.360
A true Tokyoite!

00:11:38.360 --> 00:11:40.110
What an auspicious occasion!

00:11:42.320 --> 00:11:43.240
That's too funny!

00:11:43.740 --> 00:11:45.790
Captain, what are you doing?

00:11:45.910 --> 00:11:48.290
It's a festival, so she's making merry.

00:11:50.080 --> 00:11:51.960
That kind of looks like fun.

00:11:51.960 --> 00:11:54.130
Maybe more fun than a water gun tournament.

00:11:54.670 --> 00:11:58.800
It's a festival after all,
so let's have our fill of fun!

00:11:58.800 --> 00:11:59.920
Captain...

00:12:00.430 --> 00:12:03.550
Alright, let's get excited, everyone!

00:12:11.020 --> 00:12:12.940
EQUATOR GATE

00:12:16.820 --> 00:12:20.280
This is the key that will let you
cross the equator!

00:12:24.490 --> 00:12:26.160
A round of applause!

00:12:27.410 --> 00:12:30.160
Okay, next, let's pray for safe sailing.

00:12:37.340 --> 00:12:40.170
Both of your families operate shrines, huh?

00:12:40.550 --> 00:12:42.800
That's right. Suwa Shrine.

00:12:42.800 --> 00:12:43.680
Um...

00:12:45.600 --> 00:12:46.680
Deputy-Captain?

00:12:47.140 --> 00:12:51.690
Since I have bad luck,
I was hoping you could bless me a lot?

00:12:52.730 --> 00:12:53.440
Sure.

00:12:53.650 --> 00:12:55.560
Heave-ho! Heave-ho!

00:12:55.980 --> 00:12:57.940
Heave-ho! Heave-ho!

00:13:10.500 --> 00:13:12.210
Macchi is amazing!

00:13:12.210 --> 00:13:14.540
2,000 percent seriously cool!

00:13:15.330 --> 00:13:17.290
We can't lose either!

00:13:17.460 --> 00:13:19.670
Come on! Heave-ho! Heave-ho!

00:13:19.800 --> 00:13:21.420
Heave-ho! Heave-ho!

00:13:25.470 --> 00:13:28.430
Come one, come all! Delicious takoyaki here!

00:13:28.720 --> 00:13:30.970
It even smells like a festival!

00:13:30.970 --> 00:13:32.350
What should I eat?

00:13:32.350 --> 00:13:34.800
FRANKFURTERS

00:13:33.560 --> 00:13:34.810
Hey, Isoroku!

00:13:35.230 --> 00:13:36.940
Is that pickled plum?

00:13:37.360 --> 00:13:40.230
It's a Yokosuka specialty. Cherry cheesecake.

00:13:40.230 --> 00:13:42.570
You can squeeze some lemon on top
and it's delicious.

00:13:42.570 --> 00:13:43.950
Yummy!

00:13:47.700 --> 00:13:48.700
All right!

00:13:49.120 --> 00:13:50.950
Your aim is too good!

00:13:50.950 --> 00:13:52.870
Torpedo crew aren't allowed to play.

00:13:57.580 --> 00:14:01.460
Everyone! From 7:00, we're having
performances in the classroom!

00:14:01.460 --> 00:14:03.260
We'll continue the excitement!

00:14:03.260 --> 00:14:04.260
Yeah!

00:14:06.510 --> 00:14:10.680
Two engineers are your hosts
for this evening. I'm Sora Hirota...

00:14:10.680 --> 00:14:12.100
...and I'm Reo Wakasa!

00:14:13.100 --> 00:14:15.350
We'll start with Artillery doing imitations.

00:14:15.810 --> 00:14:18.100
Ogasawara will go first!

00:14:20.980 --> 00:14:22.570
What's that supposed to be?

00:14:22.570 --> 00:14:25.110
Maybe a crying koala?

00:14:25.490 --> 00:14:28.370
That was the five-inch cannon
from an Aegis ship!

00:14:28.910 --> 00:14:30.870
- It sounded just like it!
- She's good.

00:14:31.870 --> 00:14:33.240
Takeda's next!

00:14:33.830 --> 00:14:34.830
Boom!

00:14:35.250 --> 00:14:37.040
A long ten-cm cannon! A long ten-cm cannon!

00:14:37.040 --> 00:14:37.920
Aye!

00:14:37.920 --> 00:14:39.460
Heki's up next!

00:14:39.710 --> 00:14:40.710
Boom!

00:14:41.670 --> 00:14:44.510
That was a 52 caliber, 11-inch cannon!

00:14:46.340 --> 00:14:49.050
What the heck is this? I don't get it at all!

00:14:49.930 --> 00:14:52.260
Sorry about that. Mimi's drunk on Macchi.

00:14:52.640 --> 00:14:55.230
A-All right, let's go on to our next act.

00:14:55.230 --> 00:14:56.270
Navigation!

00:14:57.440 --> 00:15:00.060
Navigation's going to do a rap for you!

00:15:02.110 --> 00:15:04.150
We're navigatin', regrettin', navigatin'!

00:15:04.440 --> 00:15:06.190
What's a wrong course you've taken?

00:15:06.490 --> 00:15:08.410
You know about my wrong course?

00:15:08.410 --> 00:15:10.200
Out in the sun, but got a sunburn!

00:15:11.320 --> 00:15:14.040
That happens! You take a wrong course!

00:15:14.120 --> 00:15:16.370
We're navigatin', navigatin', navigatin'!

00:15:16.370 --> 00:15:18.160
What's a wrong course you've taken?

00:15:18.710 --> 00:15:21.750
Me? Um... Uh...

00:15:22.420 --> 00:15:26.260
There's a drama I wanted to see,
but I forgot to hit record.

00:15:26.420 --> 00:15:28.220
What's a wrong course you've taken?

00:15:28.800 --> 00:15:30.890
Um... Uh...

00:15:30.890 --> 00:15:34.850
Gaining 425 grams while on the ship!

00:15:34.850 --> 00:15:36.180
I said it!

00:15:36.600 --> 00:15:38.310
Oh boy, that's a doubly wrong course!

00:15:38.940 --> 00:15:41.440
Leave it to the Budgeters to be precise.

00:15:42.400 --> 00:15:44.110
What's a wrong course you've taken?

00:15:44.610 --> 00:15:46.780
Oh, not me... Let's see.

00:15:47.110 --> 00:15:51.570
Before I came for training, a childhood friend
confessed romantic feelings for me,

00:15:51.570 --> 00:15:54.030
but I escaped without giving an answer.

00:15:55.990 --> 00:15:58.410
- I never heard about that before!
- Who? Who is it?!

00:15:58.660 --> 00:16:00.170
Give your answer now!

00:16:00.170 --> 00:16:01.790
Yeah, yeah!

00:16:02.420 --> 00:16:04.380
Now. Now! Let's do it now!

00:16:05.420 --> 00:16:09.300
So, I sent a text and got a response.

00:16:09.840 --> 00:16:12.050
His response, his reply, what is it?

00:16:12.050 --> 00:16:15.560
He says, "Sorry. I'm in love
with someone else now."

00:16:18.270 --> 00:16:19.640
S-Sorry.

00:16:19.640 --> 00:16:21.940
We're the ones who took the wrong course!

00:16:21.940 --> 00:16:24.520
We're navigatin', navigatin'
down the wrong course!

00:16:26.110 --> 00:16:30.070
And now, the comedic stylings of the
Chief Torpedo Officer and Chief Artillery Officer!

00:16:30.490 --> 00:16:31.570
Go ahead!

00:16:31.860 --> 00:16:35.700
- Nice to meet you! We are Meitama!
- Yes.

00:16:35.870 --> 00:16:38.160
I've been waiting for you, Meitama!

00:16:38.160 --> 00:16:39.620
Oh, Mimi...

00:16:39.620 --> 00:16:42.330
Maybe we should throw
water in her face to get her sober.

00:16:42.500 --> 00:16:44.210
The Silly Syllabary Mambo!

00:16:46.460 --> 00:16:48.090
From "A" to "Wa!"

00:16:51.930 --> 00:16:53.760
Surprised "A!"

00:16:53.760 --> 00:16:57.510
"Ah!" Look, there's cake here.
I'll just eat it. Num, num, num... Gulp.

00:16:57.510 --> 00:16:58.720
- That's rotten, you know.
- "Egh?!"

00:16:58.720 --> 00:16:59.890
- You'll hurt your stomach.
- "Ooh!"

00:16:59.890 --> 00:17:01.430
- There's a line at the bathroom.
- "Eh?"

00:17:01.430 --> 00:17:03.230
- You may not make it in time.
- "Oohh."

00:17:05.440 --> 00:17:06.610
That hits the spot!

00:17:06.610 --> 00:17:10.110
I can't believe our Chief Artillery Officer
is on stage, talking so openly.

00:17:10.110 --> 00:17:11.860
I'm moved with a big kaboom!

00:17:12.030 --> 00:17:13.860
From "A" to "Wa!"

00:17:15.370 --> 00:17:17.580
Hysterical "Ka."

00:17:17.580 --> 00:17:19.290
- Welcome home, darling.
- Hey.

00:17:19.290 --> 00:17:21.910
Ca-Caramel-colored woman's hair
on your shoulder!

00:17:21.910 --> 00:17:23.040
It must've been from the train.

00:17:23.040 --> 00:17:25.330
Kiiiiaa! A woman's lipstick!

00:17:25.330 --> 00:17:26.380
It must've been from the train.

00:17:26.380 --> 00:17:28.210
Kuuu! Your underwear is inside out!

00:17:28.210 --> 00:17:29.590
It happened on the train!

00:17:29.590 --> 00:17:30.670
Of co-urse it did.

00:17:31.260 --> 00:17:32.630
From "A" to "Wa!"

00:17:34.090 --> 00:17:36.140
Sneaky "Sa."

00:17:36.760 --> 00:17:38.390
Sa-sa-sa-sassy...

00:17:38.390 --> 00:17:39.390
Oh, shi...

00:17:42.430 --> 00:17:43.350
Captain!

00:17:44.190 --> 00:17:46.810
It's finally our turn next!

00:17:47.610 --> 00:17:48.270
Right!

00:17:48.610 --> 00:17:51.900
And now a one-act drama performed
by the members of the bridge!

00:17:51.900 --> 00:17:53.780
"The Moral Code of Harekaze."

00:17:57.530 --> 00:18:00.620
And now the Harekaze is our turf, too.

00:18:01.120 --> 00:18:03.160
It went just as planned, eh Boss?

00:18:03.500 --> 00:18:04.160
Hold it!

00:18:04.620 --> 00:18:05.790
Hold it!

00:18:07.330 --> 00:18:10.840
What's this? Harekaze bumpkins?

00:18:10.840 --> 00:18:13.670
The crew of the Harekaze may be bumpkins,

00:18:14.010 --> 00:18:16.760
but we've ain't never
taken orders from the enemy!

00:18:16.760 --> 00:18:17.680
Ain't never!

00:18:18.800 --> 00:18:21.260
- Oh. Then bring it on!
- Bring it on!

00:18:21.390 --> 00:18:22.810
I'm gonna give you a guts infusion!

00:18:23.100 --> 00:18:23.980
Boss!

00:18:24.730 --> 00:18:25.730
Guts!

00:18:26.690 --> 00:18:28.770
Shiro-boy! Speak to me!

00:18:29.060 --> 00:18:33.150
Boss, I'm countin' on you.
Gettem back for me...

00:18:33.940 --> 00:18:36.910
What's she going on about?
She's not even scratched.

00:18:38.160 --> 00:18:39.200
Kuro...

00:18:39.320 --> 00:18:40.330
Yes?

00:18:40.910 --> 00:18:45.540
I was happy earlier
when you came looking for me.

00:18:47.040 --> 00:18:52.670
Ever since we came aboard the Harekaze,
you've been stuck on Ms. Munetani.

00:18:53.760 --> 00:18:54.760
Maron...

00:18:56.130 --> 00:18:59.800
So I know how you feel right now.

00:19:01.850 --> 00:19:06.390
That's why I came up with something
I thought you might feel refreshed about.

00:19:08.940 --> 00:19:11.560
Lastly, a sumo wrestling tournament
to decide the winner!

00:19:12.070 --> 00:19:16.070
On the eastern side, Marikomaru!

00:19:16.400 --> 00:19:20.570
On the western side, Kuronofuji!

00:19:20.910 --> 00:19:23.080
Mariko's gonna win this easy.

00:19:23.080 --> 00:19:24.200
Don't be too sure.

00:19:24.950 --> 00:19:26.410
Ready in position!

00:19:26.410 --> 00:19:28.420
Go! In, in.

00:19:34.460 --> 00:19:37.170
Kuronofuji wins!

00:19:37.630 --> 00:19:40.180
A backward-twisting overarm throw!
That's some move!

00:19:40.430 --> 00:19:42.350
You sure know a lot about it, Kayo.

00:19:42.350 --> 00:19:44.180
My grandpa loves sumo.

00:19:44.430 --> 00:19:48.180
I hear Kuro won a local female
sumo wrestling tournament.

00:19:49.060 --> 00:19:50.100
Hooking backward body drop!

00:19:50.520 --> 00:19:51.600
Ankle-kicking twist down!

00:19:52.230 --> 00:19:54.520
All right, the final match at last!

00:19:54.520 --> 00:19:58.070
Engineer Assistant Hiromi Kuroki,
who's been winning smoothly

00:19:58.070 --> 00:20:00.360
with a collection
of exceptional moves, versus...

00:20:00.530 --> 00:20:05.120
who made it to the finals
through luck alone, Captain Akeno Misaki!

00:20:06.580 --> 00:20:10.120
<i>I rigged it so the Captain would
only face the weaker crew members.</i>

00:20:11.040 --> 00:20:12.830
All right, here we go!

00:20:13.080 --> 00:20:15.710
Ready in position!

00:20:16.340 --> 00:20:17.380
Go!

00:20:21.180 --> 00:20:26.600
There it is! The outer-thigh-propping twist down,
a move you may see once every decade or so!

00:20:26.970 --> 00:20:29.520
The winner, Kuronofuji!

00:20:41.950 --> 00:20:42.990
Thank you.

00:20:48.160 --> 00:20:51.290
Okay! And that's all, folks!

00:20:54.210 --> 00:20:55.920
What's wrong, Ms. Minami?

00:20:57.000 --> 00:21:00.050
I'm the only one who hasn't done anything yet.

00:21:01.590 --> 00:21:04.720
Um, do you want to do something, Ms. Minami?

00:21:04.720 --> 00:21:06.050
M-Maybe give us shots?

00:21:06.760 --> 00:21:10.810
Since it's the end, I want all of us to sing
"I am a Child of the Sea" together.

00:21:11.180 --> 00:21:14.480
Well, that's a really cute song!

00:21:14.480 --> 00:21:16.310
Not a folk song or enka.

00:21:17.150 --> 00:21:20.320
Did you used to sing it to your own kids?

00:21:20.530 --> 00:21:22.820
I am only 12 years old.

00:21:26.570 --> 00:21:28.200
- 12 years old?!
- Seriously?

00:21:28.450 --> 00:21:30.080
- It can't be!
- No way!

00:21:30.200 --> 00:21:32.080
I thought you were older than all of us.

00:21:32.330 --> 00:21:35.580
That's because I skipped several grades
and went to university.

00:21:35.580 --> 00:21:37.590
Anyway, let's sing!

00:21:37.590 --> 00:21:39.590
Everyone, please sing the chorus.

00:21:40.510 --> 00:21:48.390
I am a child of the sea, of the white waves

00:21:48.390 --> 00:21:55.690
In a pine grove, along the seashore
with the sound of waves

00:21:56.310 --> 00:22:04.030
A thin trail of smoke rising, drifting in the air

00:22:04.200 --> 00:22:11.490
That's the dear old home of mine,
where I always belong

00:22:19.040 --> 00:22:25.050
Episode 10: Happy at the Equator Festival!
